# Supply Chain Agent — environment template
#
# This file holds NO SECRETS. Anything that looks like a real credential
# is a 1Password reference (`op://vault/item/field`) that resolves at
# runtime via the 1Password CLI.
#
# Launch Claude Code from this directory with:
#
#   op run --env-file=.env -- claude
#
# `op run` reads each `op://...` reference, fetches the value from 1Password,
# and injects it into Claude Code's process environment. If a reference can't
# be resolved (vault not shared with you, item renamed, field missing),
# `op run` refuses to start — that's by design, not a bug.
#
# INSTALL.md walks through installing `op`, signing in, and verifying that
# the `AI Agents` vault is accessible.

# ── REQUIRED ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Your identity — written as `user.id` on every Langfuse trace so Pablo can
# tell your sessions apart from his. Use your GitHub handle, no `@` prefix.
# This is NOT a secret and stays as a raw value.
#
# HARD RULES (the install will refuse to proceed if violated):
#   1. Each operator MUST use their own Claude.ai account (Max sub or Teams
#      seat). Two operators sharing one Claude.ai account would collide on
#      the auto-injected `user.email` span attribute and you can't tell them
#      apart in Langfuse.
#   2. USER_ID MUST be globally unique across operators. GitHub handles work
#      because they're unique by construction.
#   3. USER_ID must NOT be `pablocreelrc` — that's reserved for Pablo's own
#      machine. Operators using his handle would alias to him in Langfuse.
USER_ID=<your-github-handle>

# Which company / engagement is this install for. Used as the `tenant` span
# attribute so Pablo can roll up traces by customer (e.g. all Sacrificio
# operators across all agents → one filter). Required.
#   - For Pablo's own machine: TENANT=internal
#   - For Sacrificio employees: TENANT=sacrificio
#   - For Desclub employees:    TENANT=desclub
#   - For Ajolote internal:     TENANT=ajolote
#   - For external SaaS clients: TENANT=<customer-slug>
TENANT=<your-company-slug>

# Langfuse observability (telemetry only, no conversation content).
#
# This Langfuse account is shared across every AI agent in the org. The
# auth header lives in a single vault item `Langfuse` so rotating the key
# updates every agent at once. Per-agent differentiation is via
# `OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` below.
CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_TELEMETRY=1
# Claude Code traces (spans) are BETA and OFF by default. Without this flag,
# only metrics and events are emitted — Langfuse's Traces tab stays empty.
CLAUDE_CODE_ENHANCED_TELEMETRY_BETA=1
OTEL_TRACES_EXPORTER=otlp
OTEL_METRICS_EXPORTER=otlp
# Langfuse does not accept OTLP logs (returns 404). Setting `none` prevents
# Claude Code from spamming a dead endpoint every 5 seconds. Span content
# (prompts, tool details/content) is included via the visibility flags below
# and rides on traces, not separate log events.
OTEL_LOGS_EXPORTER=none
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL=http/protobuf
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=https://us.cloud.langfuse.com/api/public/otel
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=op://AI Agents/Langfuse/auth_header
OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=ai-agent-ops
OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES=user.id=${USER_ID},tenant=${TENANT},deployment.environment=pilot
# Default flush is 60s; short /command sessions exit before that and lose metrics.
OTEL_METRIC_EXPORT_INTERVAL=10000

# ── DETAILED HOOK TRACING (BETA, partial pre-stage; full activation pending) ──
#
# When fully active, Claude Code emits an additional `claude_code.hook` span
# per hook execution (PreToolUse, PostToolUse, SessionStart, etc.) with
# attributes for hook_event, hook_name, num_hooks, num_success, num_blocking,
# duration_ms, and hook_definitions (gated by OTEL_LOG_TOOL_DETAILS=1).
#
# Per https://code.claude.com/docs/en/monitoring-usage (section "Traces
# (beta)"), full activation requires THREE conditions:
#   (1) ENABLE_BETA_TRACING_DETAILED=1               ← pre-staged below
#   (2) BETA_TRACING_ENDPOINT=<URL>                  ← held until Anthropic provides value
#   (3) Org allowlisted by Anthropic for interactive CLI ← request in flight
#
# (1) is safely pre-staged because the feature only activates when ALL three
# conditions are met — setting it alone is no-op. (2) is held because guessing
# a URL could route data to the wrong destination. Uncomment (2) and add the
# value Anthropic provides AFTER allowlist confirmation.
ENABLE_BETA_TRACING_DETAILED=1
# BETA_TRACING_ENDPOINT=<value provided by Anthropic on allowlisting>

# ── OPTIONAL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# All optional credentials live as fields on the per-agent vault item
# `Supply Chain Agent`. If you don't have a given credential set,
# COMMENT OUT the corresponding lines below — don't leave them pointing
# at empty vault fields. `op run` will resolve a missing field to an empty
# string, and the affected MCP server will start with empty creds and fail
# in obscure ways at runtime.
#
# The install runbook (INSTALL.md) walks through this per credential set.

# DataForSEO — SEO + competitor data + SERP snapshots.
# Used by `client-research`. Requires $50 deposit, pay-per-query.
DATAFORSEO_LOGIN=op://AI Agents/Supply Chain Agent/dataforseo_login
DATAFORSEO_PASSWORD=op://AI Agents/Supply Chain Agent/dataforseo_password

# Firecrawl — web scraping and crawling.
# Used by `client-research` and any skill that needs to scrape.
# Free 500 credits, then $16/mo.
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=op://AI Agents/Supply Chain Agent/firecrawl_api_key

# Google Workspace — Gmail / Drive / Calendar via OAuth Desktop client.
# Set up a Google Cloud project, enable Gmail / Drive / Calendar APIs,
# create an OAuth client of type "Desktop app", and store the Client ID
# and Client Secret as fields on the vault item.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=op://AI Agents/Supply Chain Agent/google_client_id
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=op://AI Agents/Supply Chain Agent/google_client_secret

# Adobe IO — Firefly (image gen), Photoshop API, Express, PDF Services.
# NOTE: Firefly Services API access requires an enterprise Adobe contract.
# Consumer Creative Cloud DOES NOT include API access. Verify your contract
# grants Firefly Services before populating the vault item.
#
# Default scope value to store in the `adobe_scope` field unless you have a
# reason to deviate (Firefly Image Generation API):
#   openid,AdobeID,session,additional_info,read_organizations,firefly_api,ff_apis
ADOBE_CLIENT_ID=op://AI Agents/Supply Chain Agent/adobe_client_id
ADOBE_CLIENT_SECRET=op://AI Agents/Supply Chain Agent/adobe_client_secret
ADOBE_SCOPE=op://AI Agents/Supply Chain Agent/adobe_scope

# ── BYO PER-EMPLOYEE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# These tools use the BYO (Bring Your Own) credential model — Pablo does NOT
# provision or send these tokens. Each employee creates their own account at
# the provider and pastes their own credential below as a RAW value (NOT an
# op:// reference). The token never leaves your machine; Pablo has no
# visibility into the data.
#
# Comment out the line for any tool you don't use. The MCP server starts with
# an empty credential and the affected MCP fails gracefully when invoked —
# see references/tools.md for per-tool setup steps.

# Monday.com — board / task tracking for client engagements and internal work.
# Get your personal API token from monday.com → avatar (bottom-left) →
# Developers → My Access Tokens → Show. Paste the raw token below.
# MONDAY_TOKEN=<your-personal-monday-api-token>
